1
00:00:17,142 --> 00:00:23,142
Bomb Voyage is a animation film directed by Robert McKimson.

2
00:00:34,285 --> 00:00:40,285
Reports of flying saucers over Paris have the Surete scrambling to keep order.

3
00:00:51,428 --> 00:00:57,428
The Commissioner is himself abducted by aliens and taken to their planet.

4
00:01:08,571 --> 00:01:14,571
Inspector Clouseau and Sergeant Deux-Deux follow in a monkey-piloted
rocket and find the Commissioner in a specimen jar.

5
00:01:25,714 --> 00:01:31,714
They release him and are chased around and around
the tiny planet by one of the aliens.

6
00:01:42,857 --> 00:01:48,857
Inspector / Sergeant Deux-Deux (voice), played by Pat Harrington, Jr..

7
00:02:00,000 --> 00:02:06,000
Commissioner (voice), played by Paul Frees.

8
00:02:17,142 --> 00:02:23,142
Dolittle is a 2020 fantasy adventure film directed by Stephen Gaghan from a screenplay by
Gaghan, Dan Gregor, and Doug Mand, based on a story by Thomas Shepherd.

9
00:02:34,285 --> 00:02:40,285
Dolittle is based on the title character created by Hugh Lofting and is primarily inspired by
the author's second Doctor Dolittle book, The Voyages of Doctor Dolittle (1922).

10
00:02:51,428 --> 00:02:57,428
Robert Downey Jr.

11
00:03:08,571 --> 00:03:14,571
stars as the title character, alongside Antonio Banderas, Michael Sheen, and Harry Collett in live-action roles, with Emma Thompson, Rami Malek, John
Cena, Kumail Nanjiani, Octavia Spencer, Tom Holland, Ralph Fiennes, Selena Gomez, and Marion Cotillard voicing an array of creatures.

12
00:03:25,714 --> 00:03:31,714
It is the third iteration of film adaptions based on the character, after the 1967
musical Doctor Dolittle starring Rex Harrison and the 1998–2009 Dr.

13
00:03:42,857 --> 00:03:48,857
Dolittle film series starring Eddie Murphy as the titular character and later Kyla Pratt as his daughter
Maya, and the only one not to be distributed by 20th Century Fox (now 20th Century Studios).

14
00:04:00,000 --> 00:04:06,000
The project was announced as The Voyage of Doctor Dolittle in March 2017 with Downey
set to star, and the rest of the cast joined over the following year.

15
00:04:17,142 --> 00:04:23,142
Filming began in March 2018 and lasted through June,
taking place around the United Kingdom.

16
00:04:34,285 --> 00:04:40,285
The film underwent three weeks of reshoots in the spring of 2019, directed by Jonathan Liebesman
and written by Chris McKay, after initial test screenings yielded poor results.

17
00:04:51,428 --> 00:04:57,428
Universal Pictures theatrically released Dolittle in
the United States on January 17, 2020.

18
00:05:08,571 --> 00:05:14,571
The film was heavily panned by film critics and grossed $251 million worldwide,
making it a box-office failure for a reported loss of $50–100 million.

19
00:05:25,714 --> 00:05:31,714
However, due to the COVID-19 pandemic, it was the
seventh highest-grossing film of 2020.

20
00:05:42,857 --> 00:05:48,857
It was nominated for six Golden Raspberry Awards, including Worst
Picture, winning for Worst Remake, Rip-off or Sequel.
